  docker/Dockerfile installs DreamZero with `pip install -e .`, which resolves
  the dependency set declared in the upstream project's pyproject.toml. That
  set is not uniformly permissive: it includes packages under GPL-3.0 (PyQt6,
  pyttsx3), LGPL-2.1 (pygame) and NVIDIA's proprietary terms (tensorrt). None
  of them is used by the training, evaluation or inference code paths in this
  repository.

  The image is built by CodeBuild into the deploying account's own ECR
  repository (cdk/dreamzero_pipeline/pipeline_stack.py) and this repository
  never publishes a prebuilt image, so no copyleft distribution obligation is
  triggered by using this sample as shipped. If you redistribute the built
